url: "https://ssrn.com/abstract=6609618"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SYMBEYOND/SYMB-FER"
abstract: "Large language models operate as stateless systems, reinitializing with each new
  conversation session. This architectural constraint creates a fundamental challenge for
  sustained human-AI collaboration: every interaction begins from zero context, requiring
  users to repeatedly establish working relationships, communication preferences, and project
  continuity. We present SYMB-FER (Symbolic Field Evidence Record), a protocol for
  transferring relational posture, identity, and operational context across stateless AI
  sessions. The protocol encodes collaboration state as structured tokens that persist
  independently of platform architecture, enabling consistent engagement patterns across
  multiple AI systems. Validation across four major LLM platforms demonstrates successful
  context transfer with cryptographic chain-of-custody verification. Real-world deployments
  include client engagements, academic collaborations, and to our knowledge, an early
  documented instance of cross-model conversational exchange."
keywords:
